Q: What is the Prayer of Manasseh in the Apocrypha?
A: It is the penitential prayer of King Manasseh of Judah while held captive in Babylon, confessing sin and appealing to the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob for the repentance promised to sinners. It survives in the Septuagint and the 1611 KJV Apocrypha.

Q: Why was the Prayer of Manasseh removed from most modern Bibles?
A: It was part of the 1611 KJV Apocrypha but was later separated from Protestant canons in the 19th century. It remains in Orthodox and some Catholic Bibles as a deuterocanonical text.

